    "overall_comment": "The translation largely preserves the line-by-line dialogue structure and most numerical and logical content, but it has notable quality problems. There is a corrupted Luc speaker label, an Arabic insertion (“بالکل”), mixed-script intrusion, untranslated English terminology, and several spelling or lexical issues. More importantly, key technical terms are repeatedly mistranslated: “wave function” is rendered as “wave product,” and amplitude is rendered as “extent/range,” affecting the scientific meaning throughout. Luc is also transliterated as “Luke,” rather than accurately representing the original name. The Kannada is generally understandable, but recurring calques and awkward formulations reduce naturalness and technical precision."
